[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4163494556","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117609#issuecomment-4163494556","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117609","id":4163494556,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc74KeKc","user":{"login":"MJacred","id":6639237,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzkyMzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6639237?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred","html_url":"https://github.com/MJacred","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-31T15:27:13Z","updated_at":"2026-03-31T15:40:25Z","body":"~~Afaict this is intentional:~~\r\n\r\n> The navigation_layers have no effect on map geometry building and how links connect to polygons. The navigation_layers are query filters. They exclude navmesh polygons or links from a query, not from a map build. The only thing that affects the map build is if a region or link is joined to a map and the enabled property is true.\r\n([Source](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102769#issuecomment-2692935239))\r\n\r\n~~Right now, even if you change the navigation layers at runtime, there's no need to rebuild the navmesh. You only need a sync. Changing this would cause unexpected behaviour if you change the navigation links layers during runtime (w/o rebaking the whole mess)~~\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n~~This issue sounds like it could be handled by selecting which navigation links to bake in the editor using a fitting baking mode, e.g. by group name: https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_navigationmesh.html#enum-navigationmesh-sourcegeometrymode~~\r\n\r\n\r\nAh, ok, seems like the change is in the sync-step…\r\n\r\n> 1. It loops through all regions without regard for navigation layers. If multiple regions have a polygon with the same closest distance, it defaults to the first region it found. Adding a check for compatible navigation layers should fix the case in my MRP. But there is another issue:\r\n> 2. It will only ever build one connection per link, even if the link would be valid for multiple pairs of regions. This looks like it would be a more involved fix, it would have to make a connection between every valid pair of regions.\r\n([Source](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117138#issuecomment-4014293745))\r\n\r\nNr 1. sounds reasonable, but I'm not convinced on Nr. 2. Could you trigger the latter one in a sensible use case?\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4163494556/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4164645264","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117609#issuecomment-4164645264","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117609","id":4164645264,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc74O3GQ","user":{"login":"BManx2000","id":13679655,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjc5NjU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13679655?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000","html_url":"https://github.com/BManx2000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-31T18:39:47Z","updated_at":"2026-03-31T18:39:47Z","body":"I did wonder if this function was supposed to consider navigation layers. Currently however, changing the navigation layers (or any property) of a link triggers a full map rebuild, so I went ahead and put the check in.\r\n\r\n> Nr 1. sounds reasonable, but I'm not convinced on Nr. 2. Could you trigger the latter one in a sensible use case?\r\n\r\nFor example, you could have a navigation layer for small agents and one for big agents, and a link representing a gap that both should be able to jump over.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4164645264/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4168878933","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117609#issuecomment-4168878933","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117609","id":4168878933,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc74fAtV","user":{"login":"MJacred","id":6639237,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzkyMzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6639237?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred","html_url":"https://github.com/MJacred","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-01T09:49:00Z","updated_at":"2026-04-01T09:49:00Z","body":"> For example, you could have a navigation layer for small agents and one for big agents, and a link representing a gap that both should be able to jump over.\r\n\r\nIn this case:  \r\nTo support multiple agent sizes, you need different regions. So you can create 1 navigation link per region and bake only the one you need.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4168878933/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4173764581","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117609#issuecomment-4173764581","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117609","id":4173764581,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc74xpfl","user":{"login":"BManx2000","id":13679655,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjc5NjU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13679655?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000","html_url":"https://github.com/BManx2000","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BManx2000/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-02T00:31:19Z","updated_at":"2026-04-02T00:31:19Z","body":"I see, so you're saying you would rather do the simple one-line fix, and make it the user's responsibility to keep the links as one-to-one relationships between regions. In that case this should be clearly documented, from the current docs it's not obvious that there is such a limitation.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4173764581/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4176344042","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117609#issuecomment-4176344042","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117609","id":4176344042,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc747fPq","user":{"login":"MJacred","id":6639237,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzkyMzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6639237?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred","html_url":"https://github.com/MJacred","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-02T10:47:02Z","updated_at":"2026-04-02T10:47:02Z","body":"Yes. For now, at least.  \r\nMaybe this PR's approach is necessary when [this one-navigation-node-to-rule-them-all](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12707) comes. Can't say for certain though.\r\n\r\nWhat I would do in this case is to close and archive this PR and open another with the one-line fix, preserving the advanced approach in case it becomes necessary.  \r\nAnd in the new PR add a note to the NavigationLink class doc regarding the one-to-one limitation.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4176344042/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]